<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC "-//W3C//DTD XHTML 1.0 Transitional//EN" "http://www.w3.org/TR/xhtml1/DTD/xhtml1-transitional.dtd">
<html xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><head><meta http-equiv="Content-Type" content="text/html; charset=UTF-8">
    <title>Security Code FAQS</title>
    <link href="@Url.Content("~/Areas/Security/Views/Styles/howtouse.css")" rel="stylesheet" type="text/css" />
</head>
<body>
    <div class="bgCont">
        <div id="page_main">
            <div id="header_cont">
                <span>Security Code FAQS</span></div>
            <div style="width: 860px; height: 310px; margin-top: 1px; font-size: 13px; text-align: justify">
                <p style="font-size: 12px; font-weight:bold;">
                    1. What is Security Code?</p>
                <p>
                    It is 6 numeric digits [0-9] and you will be asked to enter this security code each time you log-in for additional authentication.
                </p>
                
                <p style="font-size: 12px; font-weight:bold; margin-top: 25px;">
                    2. How to setup security code?</p>

                <p>
                    Input the security code and confirm it, follow the notes below.</br>

					<span style="font-style: italic;">Note:</span>
                    </br>
                    <span style="font-style:italic; margin-left:15px;">
					. Security code must be 6 numeric digits [0-9] and contains at
                    least 2 different digits.
					</span></br>
                    <span style="font-style:italic; margin-left:15px;">
					. Security code must not a ‘Forward Run or ‘Backward Run’ number 
                    ( A ‘Forward Run’ number is an integer whose digits are all in consecutive, ascending 
                    order, left to right; whereas a ‘Backward Run’ number is an interger whose digits are all in 
                    consecutive, descending order, left to right. For example: 123456, 456789, 764321, etc.. are 
                    not allowed.)
					</span>
				</p>
                
                
                <p style="font-size: 12px; font-weight:bold; margin-top: 25px;">
                    3. Does the security code expire?</p>
                
                <p>
                    It is not expired but you should change it periodically.</p>
                
                
                <p style="font-size: 12px; font-weight:bold; margin-top: 25px;">
                    4. What happens if I entered wrong security code?</p>
                <p>
                    It will require you to re-enter security code again, be noted that your account 
                    will be closed after entering the wrong security code over 5 times. Please contact your upline or 
                    CSD in this case. </p>
                    
                
                <p style="font-size: 12px; font-weight:bold; margin-top: 25px;">
                    5. What if I have forgotten my security code?</p> 
                <p>
                    Contact your upline or CSD to reset your security code. </p>
                    
               
                <p style="font-size: 12px; font-weight:bold; margin-top: 25px;">
                    6. How do I change my security code?</p>
                <p>
                    At the Home page, go to Security tab, then choose Security Code link, then change your security code. </p>
	
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>


</body></html>